1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,655
Measure your reaction time with just a ruler!

2
00:00:04,705 --> 00:00:06,625
A friend holds the end of a 30 cm ruler
upright, with 0 at the bottom

3
00:00:06,675 --> 00:00:08,775
Hold your thumb and index finger
slightly open at the 0 mark

4
00:00:08,825 --> 00:00:12,325
When your friend lets go without warning,
catch it as fast as you can!

5
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:15,845
You never know when it'll drop…

6
00:00:15,895 --> 00:00:19,215
Read the mark where you caught it

7
00:00:19,265 --> 00:00:21,415
Find that mark in the table —
that's your reaction time!

8
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:25,185
If you caught it at 15 cm,
you caught it in 0.17 seconds

9
00:00:25,235 --> 00:00:28,705
Falling things
get faster and faster

10
00:00:28,755 --> 00:00:32,675
So just from how far it fell,
you can tell how long it took

11
00:00:32,725 --> 00:00:35,845
Reaction time = the time from your eyes seeing it,
through your brain, to your hand moving

12
00:00:35,895 --> 00:00:39,415
Measure three times
and compare with your family!

13
00:00:39,465 --> 00:00:41,665
Be careful the ruler doesn't hit your face!

14
00:00:41,715 --> 00:00:44,165
NEXT: Why is summer hot?
